    "q-166802": {
      "dom_id": "question-166802",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The company used $104.7\\,\\text{ft}$ of piping to construct $5$ identical houses. Estimate the length of piping used for each home by rounding the total piping length to the nearest whole number.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{ft}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To estimate the length of piping used for each of the $5$ houses, we need to find an approximation for $104.7÷5.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n104.7\\to 105\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $105$ by $5$ as usual:\n\n$$\n105÷5=21\n$$\n\nTherefore, the construction of each house used approximately $21\\,\\text{ft}$ of pipes.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
